Native Go incremental port of pinned Apprise 1.9.9.
Original BSD-2-Clause copyright and license are retained in APPRISE-LICENSE.
Source reference: https://github.com/caronc/apprise/tree/v1.9.9

The public Certifi 2026.7.22 CA bundle and MPL-2.0 license are retained as
certifi-ca.pem and CERTIFI-LICENSE. The bundle matches the original installed
MoviePilot container SHA256 9cc2a774b5198dcff14d9be1e66091f538975d867ce029a96bce15a55dfd730f.
Source reference: https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi

Source-derived emoji patterns and IP address regular expressions retain the
original ordering and behavior. JSON URL parsing, ordered key remapping,
CPython-style ASCII JSON serialization, long-message smart splitting and the
JSON/JSONS provider are implemented in Go. Source aliases/uppercase emoji
KeyError behavior is intentionally preserved, not silently corrected.

ORIGIN.json lists the native provider schemes. The reference catalog under
testdata lists original schemes and their availability in the isolated oracle.
Valid unported schemes return ErrUnsupported. Supported providers can resolve
HTTP attachments and host-authorized local files. Invalid attachment
preparation returns False and an empty attachment list is allowed.

Pushover's Markdown-to-HTML conversion uses Goldmark v1.8.7 under the MIT
license in third_party/goldmark-LICENSE. The Go renderer adapts line breaks,
tables and code spans against the installed Python-Markdown 3.11.2 behavior.
The package requires no Python runtime.

The native HTTP port has owned wire evidence for methods, redirects, cookies,
Latin-1 headers/basic auth, TLS verification, read timeout and cancellation.
This is not a claim of full requests-library equivalence: final App authority,
netrc authentication, CA hash directories and remaining provider integration
still need original-source handling. No actual user notification was sent.
